fuzz: make Dataset::open return null for any exception from readDataset

BAG::Dataset::open() only catches H5::FileIException. Several BAG files
that are structurally valid HDF5 but have unexpected or missing attributes
cause BAG::Metadata::Metadata() (called from readDataset) to throw
BAG::ErrorLoadingMetadata or H5::AttributeIException. These exceptions
propagate uncaught through Dataset::open() into LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput,
which has no catch block, causing std::terminate() and immediate fuzzer
exit with 0 edges.

Affected seeds (confirmed locally):
  metadata_layer_example.bag  -> H5::AttributeIException
  nominal_only.bag            -> BAG::ErrorLoadingMetadata
  true_n_nominal.bag          -> BAG::ErrorLoadingMetadata

The fix adds a catch-all clause immediately after the existing
H5::FileIException catch in Dataset::open(). Any exception from
readDataset() is now caught and the function returns nullptr, which is
exactly the return value both harnesses already handle:

    auto pDataset = Dataset::open(filename, BAG_OPEN_READONLY);
    if (pDataset != NULL) { ... }   // bag_read_fuzzer.cpp line 24

Applied at BUILD TIME ONLY (mayhem/build.sh) so the upstream source in
the repo stays unmodified (the two-branch model keeps all changes additive).

diff --git a/api/bag_dataset.cpp b/api/bag_dataset.cpp
index 730d442..1f31bab 100644
--- a/api/bag_dataset.cpp
+++ b/api/bag_dataset.cpp
@@ -277,6 +277,16 @@ std::shared_ptr<Dataset> Dataset::open(
         std::cerr << "\nUnable to open BAG file: " << fileName << " due to error: " << fileExcept.getCDetailMsg();
         return nullptr;
     }
+    // mayhem: BAG::Metadata::Metadata() (called from readDataset) can throw
+    // BAG::ErrorLoadingMetadata or H5::AttributeIException for BAG files that are
+    // valid HDF5 but have unexpected/missing attributes. These propagate uncaught
+    // through LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput, causing std::terminate() and 0-edge runs.
+    // Catch everything here and return nullptr -- the same contract both harnesses
+    // already handle for the H5::FileIException case above.
+    catch (...)
+    {
+        return nullptr;
+    }

     return pDataset;
 }
